<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African liquidations up sharply in Jun-Sept.</title>
<headline>S.African liquidations up sharply in Jun-Sept.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African company liquidations increased by 17.2 percent in the quarter ended 30 September 1996, the Central Statistical Service (CSS) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The CSS said liquidations increased from 690 in the previous quarter to 809 in the June-Sept quarter.</p>
<p>It attributed the increase to a substantial increase in compulsory liquidations.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
